{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791051540,"nonce":"sW1Mb8jTxtIVZjpaNo9Ql17gOFM=","title":"Impl method return types are recorded only when their impl lowers","message":"LoweringContext records a free function's return type in function_return_types during collect_declarations, but an impl method's (Type$method) only in lower_impl_block. A function lowered before the impl that declares a method it calls cannot type `let q = p.m()` from the method (resolve_expr_type finds no entry), so a later q.n() is an analysis error and the function is dropped (\"Cannot resolve method 'n' on unknown type\"). Host-module declarations work around it by going ahead of the program's own. collect_declarations should record impl method return types too. Separately, the type checker has no method lookup for Type::Extern receivers (resolve_method returns None for them), which strict mode reports as \"method not found\" on every extern method call.","files":null}]}